      "latency_ms": 12690.6,
      "prompt_tokens": 25,
      "completion_tokens": 1151,
      "output": "\n\nWater is a chemical substance composed of two hydrogen atoms and one oxygen atom, chemically represented as **H₂O**. It is a vital component of life and one of the most abundant and unique substances on Earth. Here's a breakdown of its key characteristics:\n\n### **Chemical Structure**\n- **Molecular Composition**: Each water molecule consists of two hydrogen atoms covalently bonded to one oxygen atom, forming a bent (V-shaped) structure. This arrangement creates a polar molecule, with partial positive charges on the hydrogen atoms and a partial negative charge on the oxygen atom.\n- **Hydrogen Bonding**: Water molecules attract each other through hydrogen bonds, which are weaker than covalent bonds but strong enough to influence its physical properties (e.g., high boiling point, surface tension).\n\n### **Physical Properties**\n- **State of Matter**: At standard temperature and pressure, water is a liquid. It can exist as a solid (ice) or gas (water vapor) under different conditions.\n- **Unique Anomalies**: \n  - **Density**: Ice is less dense than liquid water, allowing it to float. This is critical for aquatic ecosystems in cold climates.\n  - **High Specific Heat**: Water absorbs and releases heat slowly, helping regulate temperature in organisms and the environment.\n  - **High Heat of Vaporization**: It requires significant energy to evaporate, which is why sweating cools the body.\n\n### **Role in Nature and Life**\n- **Hydrosphere**: Water covers about 71% of Earth's surface, forming oceans, lakes, rivers, and groundwater. Most of it is saltwater, with only ~2.5% being freshwater.\n- **Water Cycle**: It cycles through evaporation, condensation, precipitation, and runoff, distributing water globally and sustaining ecosystems.\n- **Biological Necessity**: All known life forms depend on water. It acts as a **solvent** for biochemical reactions, a **transport medium** for nutrients and waste, and a **temperature regulator** in organisms.\n\n### **Unique Characteristics**\n- **Universal Solvent**: Water dissolves more substances than any other liquid, facilitating nutrient absorption and chemical reactions in living systems.\n- **Cohesion and Adhesion**: Molecules stick to each other (cohesion) and to other surfaces (adhesion), enabling processes like capillary action in plants.\n\nIn summary, water is a simple yet extraordinary molecule whose unique properties make it indispensable for life, environmental stability, and countless natural processes. Its ability to exist in multiple states, form hydrogen bonds, and support biological functions sets it apart from other substances."
    },
